{"base_rate":0.36268068331143233,"brier":0.13461340341655714,"bss":0.41761953682952346,"bss_hi":0.5125746030690211,"bss_lo":0.31101378591840784,"country":"CH","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.085676741130092,"ess":390.36265668425006,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Geneva</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Geneva rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGENEVE COINTRIN, 5.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.42, ranked 28 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(11&ndash;60) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>278</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>101</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>231</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Geneva</b> <span class=\"muted\">CH</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.42</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>11&ndash;60\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Geneva &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Geneva\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 82.56970297029703,338.7524752475248 169.4864,226.69333333333333 295.2265789473684,99.42105263157896 405.71688311688314,19.575757575757564 405.71688311688314,30.606060606060623 295.2265789473684,176.05263157894737 169.4864,304.3466666666667 82.56970297029703,371.18811881188117 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"249.98423127463863\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"249.98423127463863\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,375.45323741007195 82.56970297029703,324.33663366336634 169.4864,255.81333333333333 295.2265789473684,152.10526315789474 405.71688311688314,96.78787878787881\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 278 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"375.45323741007195\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 101 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"82.56970297029703\" cy=\"324.33663366336634\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"169.4864\" cy=\"255.81333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"295.2265789473684\" cy=\"152.10526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 231 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"405.71688311688314\" cy=\"96.78787878787881\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(36%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Geneva the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.59) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.17).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.167</td><td class='num'>18.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.322</td><td class='num'>8.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.526</td><td class='num'>5.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.585</td><td class='num'>5.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":46.20222,"lon":6.14569,"n":761,"n_cities":109,"name":"Geneva","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":278,"obs":0.017985611510791366,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.06940594059405941,"n":101,"obs":0.15841584158415842,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.3149333333333334,"n":75,"obs":0.3466666666666667,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.5,"mean":0.6701315789473684,"n":76,"obs":0.631578947368421,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9822510822510823,"n":231,"obs":0.7835497835497836,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.4,"rank":28,"rank_hi":60.02499999999998,"rank_lo":10.975000000000001,"reliability":0.013402104102108027,"resolution":0.10995577734359205,"slug":"geneva","station":"GENEVE COINTRIN","timezone":"Europe/Zurich"}